{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And HaShem has made you declare.</b> That is, He too performed for you such signs and wonders as you saw with your own eyes, until He brought it about that you declared you would be to Him a treasured people, as He spoke to you — that is, at Sinai; this is what is said (Exodus 19): ״אם שמוע תשמעו בקולי ושמרתם את בריתי והייתם לי סגולה מכל העמים״. <br><b>And to keep all His commandments,</b> on condition that you keep His commandments, for the distinction of Israel in being called by the name 'treasured' is only through the keeping of the commandments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:20.368628353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}